UID:fN5ed3NQFc
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 123 mins (2h03m)\n\nOscar® winner Scandar Copti (Aj
 ami) is back with a new film about a middle-class Arab family in Israel an
 d the impact of the country’s divisions on every aspect of their lives\,
  mundane and momentous alike.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/happy-holid
 ays
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Odd Fish
DTSTART:20250522T224500Z
DTEND:20250523T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T224500Z
UID:7a9AbHqyaS
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 104 mins (1h44m)\n\nIn this gentle and welcoming dra
 medy—the first Icelandic film to feature a trans female lead—two child
 hood besties who co-run a seafood restaurant in the northern Westfjords ha
 ve their friendship tested when one of them comes out. This film is genero
 usly sponsored by Jeff Stolz and Tim O'Connor. Also sponsored by:\n\nhttps
 ://www.siff.net/festival/odd-fish
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Luz
DTSTART:20250523T013000Z
DTEND:20250523T032500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T013000Z
UID:YhGlf5G2jE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nA Chinese ex-con seeks to rekind
 le a relationship with his estranged cam girl daughter\, while a gallerist
  connects with her ailing French stepmother (Huppert)\, in this dual narra
 tive about finding familial intimacy in a virtual reality world. Sponsored
  by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/luz
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
